  <p>That 5MB figure is worth a sentence. It is a real Weibo number, but from the API documents that govern apps posting on a user's behalf. It was never the limit for someone posting through Weibo itself, and the guides that carried it had not read the help center.</p>

  <h2>What are the Weibo ad placement sizes?</h2>

  <p>There is no readable answer from Weibo.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Weibo's advertising help center served no specification text to an open request on 10 September 2026. The ad creative figures in circulation, among them a 5M image cap, five accepted image ratios from 3:4 to 16:9, and a one-minute ceiling for vertical video ads, trace to a single 2023 page repeated across several sites. Treat them as one published account and confirm in the ad account before building.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: direct fetch of tui.weibo.com on 10 September 2026, plus 1 origin page carried on 3 sites, Chinese-language. Contested, not a platform reading.</p>

  <p>One page copied three times is one source. Those figures are a starting point for a conversation with the ad account manager, not a spec to build a campaign to.</p>

  <h2>Why this page exists</h2>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Five English searches for Weibo image, video, grid and ad specifications returned one Weibo-specific guide, dated 2022. It carries no video specification, no 18-image ceiling and no crop mechanism. Not one English result cited Weibo's help center, which answers several of those questions openly.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: 5 English queries run 10 September 2026, every result classified by page type and date. An observation about published sources.</p>

  <p>The <a href="/services/design/social-media">social media design service page</a> covers producing across the Chinese social platforms, the <a href="/resources/insights/rednote-note-cover-specs">article on RedNote note and cover specs</a> covers the platform with the most contested crop rules, and the <a href="/resources/insights/douyin-video-specs-safe-zones">article on Douyin video specs and safe zones</a> covers vertical video.</p>

  <p>Reviewed 10 September 2026. Confirm every counted figure in your own account before building a batch to it.</p>

  <h2>Questions about Weibo specs</h2>

  <h3>What size should a Weibo post image be?</h3>

  <p>Weibo's help center, updated 1 April 2026, says each image must be under 20M in GIF, JPG or PNG, while a May 2025 help page says images over 30M get compressed. No pixel size is published. Because the grid shows square tiles, a square upload is the one shape no published crop account changes.</p>

  <h3>How does the Weibo nine-grid crop images?</h3>

  <p>Sources agree the grid shows square tiles, but only one describes the mechanism, a center crop, and it is about eight years old. Weibo's 2026 help page adds a focus point without saying what it controls. Uploading square images avoids the question, and keeping the ninth tile's lower right corner clear protects the hidden-image count.</p>

  <h3>What are the Weibo video specs?</h3>

